DATA LICENSE — data/db.json

The geographic data in this package (data/db.json, and the copy bundled
into dist/) is derived from:

  Myanmar Information Management Unit (MIMU)
  Myanmar Place Codes (P-codes), Release 9.7, January 2026
  https://themimu.info/place-codes

Place names are from the General Administration Department (GAD) and field
sources, transliterated by MIMU (except the Naga Self-Administered Zone).

This data is NOT covered by the ISC license in LICENSE. It remains subject
to MIMU's own terms, which state:

  - Use constraints: acknowledgement of the Myanmar Information Management
    Unit (MIMU) as the source.
  - MIMU products are not for sale and not for commercial use. They can be
    used free of charge with attribution.
  - The names shown and the designations used do not imply official
    endorsement or acceptance by the United Nations.

If you use or redistribute this data, credit MIMU as the source, for
example: "Place names and codes: MIMU P-codes 9.7 (themimu.info)".
You are responsible for checking that your use fits MIMU's terms; contact
info.mimu@undp.org with questions.

Changes made by this package: Bago and Shan are presented as single states
(MIMU's parts are kept as `partCodes`); only places MIMU marks as active
are included; names are Unicode-normalized (NFC) with zero-width characters
removed; slugs and 1.x slug aliases are added; state coordinates and
capitals come from mmgeo 1.x, not MIMU.

MAP OUTLINES — data/map.json

The outlines used by `@tm11/mmgeo/map` and `@tm11/mmgeo/boundaries` are
currently built from Natural Earth 1:10m Admin-1 (states and provinces),
https://www.naturalearthdata.com, which is in the public domain. Natural
Earth folds Nay Pyi Taw into Mandalay Region, so it has no outline of its own.
They are simplified and projected by scripts/build-map.ts.

